IMPORTANT: The Passport Agency has a limited number of Emergency
Processing Slots (EPS). If your departure date is in 5 business days
or less, you must call Passport Express immediately at (800) 362-8196
 to reserve an EPS.
STEP 1 - Gather US Passport Application Materials
 A) Letter of Authorization (2 copies)

 Age 18 and older, click for Leer of Authorization, print 2 copies,
 close form window.
 Age 16 & 17 passport applicants, select Child Letter of Authorization,
 print 2 copies, close form window.
 B) Order Form

 aide for Order Form, print 1 copy, close form window.
 C) Two Passport Photos

 MallBoxes Etc., Kinkos Copies and AAA provide passport photos, or
 consult yellow pages under "Photographers-Passport."Do NOT use vending
 machine or your own photos.
 D) Proof of US Citizenship

  Include one of the following.
  Old Passport (undamaged),OR
  Offidal government-issued Birth Certificate (if born In the US), OR
  FS-240, DS-1350, or Certificate of Citizenship (if born abroad to US
  parent(s)), OR
   Naturalization Papers (for U.S.citizens through naturalization)
   Proof of citizenship must be an original or certified copy. No
   photocopies or notarized copies are accepted.
   The original document will be returned to you with your completed passport.
   E) Proof of Identity

  A Photocopy of the applicant's Valid Driver's License, Issued more
  than 6 months ago.
  If applicant does not possess a valid photo driver's license (state ID
  cards/military ids are not enough), or if license was Issued less than
  6 months ago (even renewals), dick for additional Proof of Identity
  instructions.
• Applicants age 16 or 17 without a valid, 6 month old driver's license,
   can have a parent co-sign the application. In this case, a birth
   certificate proving parental relationship is required for the
   application.

