     /Travel Evidence (include 2 copies of one of the following)

    copy of plane ticket showing foreign departure, OR
/   copy of travel itinerary (from airline or travel agency with applicant
    name, travel date, flight info), OR
    if travel is for business and neither of above is available, see
    business travel letters
    G) DS-11 & DS-64 Government Forms

    The DS-64 can be downloaded here.
    Click here to fill out the DS-11
    You MUST fill out this form electronically and then print 2 copies
    Fin out all of the fields on the form.
    Click on the "create form" button to generate the completed form.
    Print at least TWO copies of the form.
    Do not sign the form until you appear in front of your local passport
    Acceptance Agent (see step 2)
    Call us if you have any problems with this form.
    Both forms are necessary.
    Confirm that the "Mail Passport To" field on the government form is
    completed with the actual address where you want the completed
    passport FedExed (no PO boxes).
    The government can insist that your completed passport be sent to the
    address that you have listed on your form, even if you give us a
     different address on your order form.
    The government can choose to send your passport back to you via
    regular mail if the addresses do not match.
     There is no way for us to verify the address that you have listed,
     thus we cannot be responsible for any delays associated with this
          ic-tion
     Please call with any questions.
     Hj Fees(all fees are paid in separate checks)

     Government Payment (2 seperate checks)
     $30 collected by your local Acceptance Agent (explained below)
     $127 check payable to Department of State
     Check to Passport Express
     $199 for Urgent Service.
     $100 Emergency Processing Slot (EPS) fee for travel in 4 business days
     or less. NOTE: Copy of plane ticket or travel itinerary required.
     Reserve EPS at (800) 362-8196 immediately if traveling this quickly.
     $20 return S&I-1 for weekday FedEx delivery $35 for Saturday.
                                                                                                ***
     *******************************************************************************************

     What Business Travel Letter Must Include:
     Travel date must be more than 3 business days up to 3 weeks in order
     to use a "business travel letter" as Travel Evidence

     Business Travel Letters used as Travel Evidence must be on company letterhead.

     Tne letter must state the following:
     Name of passport applicant
     Country of travel
     The purpose and urgent nature of the trip
     Specific international departure date. Do NOT use "ASAP" or any "on or
     about" type statements. If departure date is not finalized, be
     conservative and list the earliest date travel may occur.
     Departure time and time the applicant must leave for the airport
     should also be listed if known along with any flight information
     (airline, flight #, etc.)
     The letter must be signed by someone other than the applicant.
